# check_supabase_table_refs.sh allowlist — table names that look like orphans
# but are NOT actually broken references. One name per line. Comments start
# with #. Each entry MUST have a comment above it explaining WHY it's exempt.
# Adding new entries requires James approval.
#
# Removing entries requires verifying the underlying issue is resolved.

# [removed 2026-05-05 dumps Phase B] `dumps` was a Supabase Storage bucket,
# not a Postgres table. Phase A audit confirmed all 3 references are
# `supabase.storage.from('dumps')`. The script's awk extractor was tightened
# to filter `.storage.from(...)` references — `dumps` is no longer detected
# as a candidate at all, so the allowlist entry was removed (not just kept
# perma-suppressed). See `docs/audit/2026-05-05-dumps-orphan-phase-a.md`.

# `messages` — referenced by calculate-importance but absent from PostgREST
# schema despite migration `20251122051423` creating it in public. Possibly
# RLS-filtered (PostgREST hides RLS-locked tables from anon role) or
# schema-cache stale. Pending separate audit. Same status as `dumps`.
messages
